  "rationale": "Rahsaan Roland Kirk's masterpiece — a defining statement of his multi-instrumental, post-bop approach. Consensus across independent listing traditions: AllMusic 5★, Penguin Guide to Jazz Recordings 3.5★, Pitchfork #170 on '200 Best Albums of the 1960s'. The album showcases Kirk's full instrumental arsenal (tenor sax, manzello, stritch, clarinet, flute, whistle, English horn, flexatone) and features the classic quartet with Rahn Burton, Steve Novosel, and Jimmy Hopps, plus Dick Griffin's trombone on 'Fly by Night'. It reached #19 on Billboard Jazz Albums chart and remains Kirk's most celebrated studio statement.",
